<section class="section-new bg-gray">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="section-label text-center">FAQ</span>
        <h2 class="text-center">5 common questions about cross-border e-commerce</h2>
        <div class="top-faq">
            <details>
                <summary>Which payment methods are supported?<span class="acc-icon">+</span></summary>
                <div class="top-faq-answer">Credit cards (Visa and Mastercard). For B2B commerce, bank transfers and invoice payments are also supported.</div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Which countries can I sell to?<span class="acc-icon">+</span></summary>
                <div class="top-faq-answer">Leap supports 22 major countries and regions.
                    <dl>
                        <dt>Americas (4)</dt><dd>United States, Canada, Mexico, Brazil</dd>
                        <dt>Europe (6)</dt><dd>United Kingdom, Germany, France, Italy, Spain, Netherlands</dd>
                        <dt>Asia-Pacific (12)</dt><dd>Japan, Australia, Singapore, Mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong, South Korea, Vietnam, Philippines, Malaysia, Indonesia, India</dd>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Which currencies are supported?<span class="acc-icon">+</span></summary>
                <div class="top-faq-answer">US dollars, euros, and Japanese yen.</div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Can I sell different products in different countries?<span class="acc-icon">+</span></summary>
                <div class="top-faq-answer">Yes. You can choose which countries each product is sold in, and it won’t appear in other countries.</div>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>How are exchange rates handled?<span class="acc-icon">+</span></summary>
                <div class="top-faq-answer">Choose one base currency for each product. Prices are converted automatically at the previous day’s exchange rate and shown in other currencies, updated daily.</div>
            </details>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

